{
  "id": "29392_ninshinsuru",
  "headword": "{妊娠|にんしん}する",
  "reading": "にんしんする",
  "romaji": "ninshinsuru",
  "part_of_speech": "suru verb",
  "gloss": "to become pregnant; to conceive",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to become pregnant; to conceive",
      "explanation": "To become pregnant; to conceive a child. Used of the woman who is pregnant."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29392_ninshinsuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{彼女|かのじょ}は{妊娠|にんしん}している。",
      "english": "She is pregnant.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29392_ninshinsuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{妻|つま}が{妊娠|にんしん}したと{聞|き}いて{喜|よろこ}んだ。",
      "english": "I was delighted to hear my wife had become pregnant.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29392_ninshinsuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{妊娠|にんしん}してからは、{食事|しょくじ}に{気|き}をつけるようになった。",
      "english": "Since becoming pregnant, she's started paying attention to her diet.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: usually {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive); the woman is the subject. The child carried may optionally be marked with を: {子|こ}どもを{妊娠|にんしん}する.\n\nASPECT: {妊娠|にんしん}している describes the ongoing state of being pregnant, while {妊娠|にんしん}した marks the moment of becoming pregnant.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {妊娠|にんしん}{中|ちゅう}: during pregnancy\n- {妊娠|にんしん}{初期|しょき}: early pregnancy\n- {妊娠|にんしん}が{分|わ}かる: to find out one is pregnant",
